  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two identical charged spheres are suspended by strings of equal lengths. The strings make an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> with each other. When suspended in water the angle remains the same. If density of the material of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>cc</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the dielectric constant of water will be ______.</p><p>(Take density of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>cc</mi></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/861fab98-5938-470d-8be7-bf274f340afe.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 223px;\"/></p><p>In air:</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>In water:</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>mg</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Equate both equations, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
